### Everything is excluded, then the few things the image needs are let back in. An allowlist and
### not a blocklist on purpose: the credentials in .env must never reach the build context, and a
### blocklist protects only against the files someone thought of.
*

### The packaged application (fast-jar layout). Build it first: ./mvnw clean package
### The directory is named as well as its contents: an excluded directory is not descended into,
### so re-including only the contents can leave nothing to find.
!target/quarkus-app
!target/quarkus-app/**

### The embedding model, ~482 MB, copied as its own image layer. Not in Git; fetch it once with
### scripts/download-embedding-model.sh. Without these lines the build fails at COPY rather than
### producing an image that starts and then cannot embed anything.
!models
!models/**
